const FEATS_OSH=[
  {name:'Acrobat',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',desc:'You are nimble and graceful enough to be a circus performer. Gain a Free Re-roll to run, jump, balance, and perform feats of acrobatics.'},
  {name:'Barrier',book:'osh',trigger:'Full Turn',adr:true,desc:'You can summon or create impenetrable barriers. You can use your strength or powers to stop incoming water or flames, to protect yourself or your group from the wind, or to contain a small explosion. Indestructible Barrier [Full Turn]: spend 1 Adrenaline to summon a barrier that grants Total Cover to yourself and 4 other people. The barrier can withstand anything, and lasts as long as you remain still and focused.'},
  {name:'Bulletproof',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',desc:'Your body is made of stone or metal, or your skin and bones are as tough as duramantium. You are completely immune to damage from firearms (but not from energy weapons or explosive weapons). During a shootout, a friend can use you as Partial Cover.'},
  {name:'Bullseye',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',desc:'Every shot hits its mark. Gain a Free Re-roll to hit a target with precision using a small object or ranged weapon.'},
  {name:'Cyborg',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',adr:true,desc:'Part of your body was replaced by a hyper-technological prosthesis, or you are a fully synthetic being. Gain a Free Re-roll to all Fix rolls. It takes a Fix roll instead of a Heal roll to remove the Hurt Condition from you. Solid Metal: spend 1 Adrenaline to repeat a failed Reaction Roll.'},
  // Detective: unified core/osh entry lives in the main FEATS array (tagged books:['core','osh']).
  {name:'Energy Manipulation',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',desc:'You can use your powers to hone pure energy into a weapon. Gain the Energy Blade (Melee Weapon, Perfect) and Energy Bolt (Energy Weapon) super-weapons; an Energy Blade can represent any melee weapon made of pure energy. You can choose this Feat twice — if you do, your Energy Bolt also gains the Maximum Power Feat.'},
  {name:'Familiar',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',desc:'You never leave your friend behind. You have a small animal, magical creature, friendly robot, or another friendly familiar. Your familiar takes a small Quick Action every Turn and always tries to Help you however it can. The familiar shares your Grit and can never be Left for Dead.'},
  {name:'Flight',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',desc:'You can control gravity around you, or have a beautiful set of wings. You can fly freely and hover. In most cases, the skill used to fly fast or with agility is Stunt.'},
  {name:'Foresight',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',adr:true,desc:'You already know what they’re about to say. Once per Session, predict the outcome of an action taken by yourself or a friend and choose to alter it: once the Director describes the outcome, you may let your vision come true and keep playing, “rewind” and choose a different course of action, or warn your friends. Read Your Opponent: when an Enemy uses a Special Action in combat, spend an amount of Adrenaline equal to the level of the action to stop them before it can go through.'},
  {name:'Gadget',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',desc:'You have a weapon or object of hyper-technological, magical, or legendary origin. Choose and gain one Gadget of any kind from the gadget list. You can choose this Feat more than once.'},
  {name:'Giant Growth',book:'osh',trigger:'Full Turn',adr:true,desc:'You can increase your size beyond measure, becoming an actual giant. When you have the peace and quiet to do it (e.g. during a Time-Out), you can become a giant to easily carry out otherwise difficult actions, like building a barricade, clearing rubble, or raising a dam. Giant Form [Full Turn]: spend 1 Adrenaline to quickly turn into a giant. While a giant, your Brawn score is always 5; every time you would lose Grit, you instead lose half that amount (rounded up). Due to your size you become extremely slow and heavy: you automatically fail all rolls in Crime, and you can only act once every other Action Turn (but still take all Reaction Turns). You return to normal when you run out of Grit, become Broken or Powerless, when you reach the end of the Scene, or whenever you choose. When you drop Giant form, you become Tired; if you are already Tired, you become Broken.'},
  // Hacker: unified core/osh entry lives in the main FEATS array (tagged books:['core','osh']).
  {name:'Immortality',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',desc:'You are practically immortal. When you are Left for Dead, you fall into a state of apparent death. Once per Turn, you can flip a coin; if the result is Tails, you come back to life, ready for action. When you revive, you recover 1 Grit and can brush off one Condition of your choice. If you are cut to pieces or buried, it takes you two days to get yourself back together or regenerate from your head.'},
  {name:'Incorporeal',book:'osh',trigger:'Full Turn',adr:true,desc:'Walls, doors, safes — nothing can keep you out. You can use one Full Turn to move through a wall, floor, or other solid surface as if it were made of air. Phase Shift: spend 1 Adrenaline to instantly become incorporeal (for example when running or falling) without using up your Turn. Alternatively, dodge one melee attack without rolling.'},
  {name:'Invisible',book:'osh',trigger:'Quick Action',desc:'Now I see you. Now I don’t. As a Quick Action, you can turn fully invisible, or return visible. While invisible, gain a Help for all rolls to avoid being located. During combat, if you opt not to attack the Enemy on your Action Turn, you cause them to lose track of you and skip the next Reaction Turn. You stop being invisible when you lose 2 or more Grit in one hit, suffer any Condition, or choose to.'},
  {name:'Jump',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',adr:true,desc:'You flex your muscles and throw yourself on the enemy. You can make extremely long or high jumps, and you never lose Grit when falling from a height. Leap Attack: spend 1 Adrenaline to jump onto a distant or flying enemy and attack them as if you were in melee — gain +1 and a Free Re-roll for this attack.'},
  {name:'Lord of the Seas',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',adr:true,desc:'You can do more than talk to fish… but yes, you talk to fish. In water, gain a Free Re-roll to all rolls, plus a Help to swim, and you can breathe underwater just fine. You can communicate with fish and other sea-dwelling creatures. Call of the Sea [Quick Action]: spend 1 Adrenaline to call on one or several sea creatures to come to your side and Help however they can.'},
  {name:'Mind Control',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',adr:true,desc:'You can control other people with the force of your mind or magic. Gain a Free Re-roll to persuade someone to cooperate or help you. Puppet [Full Turn]: spend 1 Adrenaline to take control of a supporting character and move them however you like. You can’t ask the controlled person to do something that harms them, directly or indirectly. You lose control of the puppet when you lose Grit, suffer a Condition, or lose focus. To take control of an Enemy (or an individual in a group of Enemies), make an Action Roll with difficulty equal to the Enemy Defense.'},
  {name:'Monster',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',desc:'People look at you with fear or suspicion. Your inhuman appearance gives a Hindrance when you speak or interact with people who don’t know you, and grants a Help to all rolls to intimidate.'},
  {name:'Multiple Hero',book:'osh',trigger:'Full Turn',desc:'You can split or multiply into copies of yourself at will. During a Time-Out, you can create copies of yourself to gain an extra action. Multiplication [Full Turn]: roll Smooth+Endure to multiply yourself — create 1 copy for every Basic Success, 3 copies for every Critical Success, and 9 copies for every Extreme Success. Each copy has limited strength and can only take a Quick Action each Turn. Each copy also counts as an additional point of Grit — every time you lose Grit, you can choose to sacrifice an equal number of copies to avoid the loss. Copies dissolve after being hit, when they get too far from you, when you dismiss them, when you suffer Powerless, or automatically at end of Scene. When all your copies dissolve, you become Tired; if already Tired, you become Broken.'},
  {name:'New Powers',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',desc:'You have just gained or discovered a new power. Gain a new Superpower of your choice, with the exception of Invincible or One of a Kind. You can choose this Feat only if it makes sense in the story and all Players agree to it.'},
  {name:'Only Weakness',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',desc:'If the enemy learns about your weakness, it’s over for you. You have a weakness — your powers could be tied to an artifact that can be stolen, or there’s a space crystal out there that can weaken you. You may choose your weakness, or leave it up to the Director. When you’re exposed to your weakness, you suffer the Powerless Condition. This Feat can be chosen only at character creation. If you do, you gain another Feat of your choice. If you gained this Feat from the Invincible Superpower, you do NOT gain an extra Feat.'},
  {name:'Personal A.I.',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',desc:'You have a personal A.I. based in your super-suit, in an accessory (perhaps your watch or stylish glasses), or you are a hyper-developed A.I. yourself. Access the A.I. database to ask questions about general knowledge, history, geography, and other topics. The A.I. also lets you track and get a lock on nearby enemies, and grants Help when you need to quickly analyze the layout of a city or the plan of a building to find an escape route.'},
  {name:'PhD',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',desc:'They don’t just hand out degrees like yours. Choose one field of study you specialize in (e.g. engineering, medicine, astrophysics). Gain a Free Re-roll for all rolls regarding your chosen degree.'},
  {name:'Pint-Sized',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',desc:'You’re about half as tall as a human, possibly less. Gain a Free Re-roll to all Stealth rolls and to dodge projectiles. Additionally, gain a Help to all rolls made to squeeze into narrow spaces or go unnoticed.'},
  {name:'Power Absorption',book:'osh',trigger:'Full Turn',desc:'You can copy the powers of your friends or enemies. If you so much as touch someone with superpowers, you run the risk of hurting them and giving them the Powerless Condition. Stolen Power [Full Turn]: when you touch an ally with superpowers, you can steal their Superpower and all connected Feats until end of Scene — you gain all the stolen Superpowers, but your friend temporarily becomes Powerless. You can use this on an Enemy only if you manage to completely disable them for one Turn; if you succeed, the Director determines the extent of the powers you steal based on the Enemy Feats.'},
  {name:'Power-Mirror',book:'osh',trigger:'Quick Action',adr:true,desc:'You can copy the powers of your friends or enemies. Thanks to your ability to copy other people’s powers, you can use one of your actions during a Time-Out to help a friend who is trying to Show Off their Superpower. Borrowed Power [Quick Action]: when you touch someone with superpowers, spend 1 Adrenaline to immediately use one of their special actions, or to temporarily gain the benefits of their Superpower.'},
  {name:'Prep Time',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',adr:true,desc:'No matter the situation, you always come prepared. Once per Session, ask the Director for information about a location or person. Prepared: once per combat, after an Enemy reveals one of their Feats, spend 1 Adrenaline to pull out an accessory or strategy to counteract it — the Enemy loses that Feat until end of Scene.'},
  {name:'Regeneration',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',adr:true,desc:'You have a regenerative factor that allows you to heal any wound easily. Whenever you would lose 3 or more Grit from an Enemy or another physical danger, you lose 1 less Grit. Fast Recovery [Quick Action]: spend 1 Adrenaline to recover 3 Grit or heal from the Tired or Hurt Condition.'},
  {name:'Shrinkage',book:'osh',trigger:'Full Turn',adr:true,desc:'You can shrink all the way down to the size of a tiny ant without sacrificing physical strength. Shrinking requires a Full Turn. While shrunk, gain a Help to all rolls made to squeeze into narrow spaces or go unnoticed. Instant Miniaturization: spend 1 Adrenaline to shrink on the spot — break free from any grapple or restraints, automatically succeed a Reaction Roll during combat, or pass another Reaction Roll the Director deems relevant. Instant Enlargement: while shrunk, spend 1 Adrenaline to return to your original size on the spot and attack an Enemy with +1 and a Free Re-roll.'},
  {name:'Sonic Boom',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',desc:'Your voice has terrible destructive power. With the power of your voice or the sonic waves you emit, you can destroy objects and barriers. Gain the Sonic Wave super-weapon (Energy Weapon, Impact). You can choose this Feat twice — if you do, your Sonic Wave also gains the Maximum Power Feat.'},
  {name:'Speak with Animals',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',adr:true,desc:'You understand animals, and they understand you. You can speak with animals of all kinds and species. Call of the Wild [Quick Action]: spend 1 Adrenaline to call on the animals in the area — they come to you and Help to the best of their ability.'},
  {name:'Super Senses',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',adr:true,desc:'Nothing can elude your hyper-developed senses. Gain a Free Re-roll for all Reaction Rolls in combat and for all rolls made to sense danger, prevent an ambush, or spot lurking enemies. Attention: spend 1 Adrenaline to repeat a failed Detect or Awareness Roll.'},
  {name:'Super-Ride',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',adr:true,desc:'You can rely on a hyper-technological, magical, or alien ride at your beck and call. You have a super-ride of your choice (see Rides in Section 6: Weapons & Gear). Gain a Free Re-roll to all rolls made to drive your super-ride. Ride Recall [Quick Action]: spend 1 Adrenaline to recall or summon your super-ride — it reaches you, or comes as close as possible.'},
  {name:'Team Leader',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',desc:'Your comrades look to you to guide them and help them through the darkness. Gain a Free Re-roll to inspire and coordinate others, and to all rolls made to remove the Like a Fool and Defeated Conditions. When Heroes assemble, make a heartfelt speech to your group to raise the starting Teamwork to 2.'},
  {name:'Trained Fighter',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',desc:'You’ve been through your fair share of battles, but it’s not time to rest yet. Choose one fighting style or melee weapon (e.g. hand-to-hand combat, batons, katana). Gain a Free Re-roll for all Action and Reaction Rolls made with your chosen style or weapon.'},
  {name:'Transformation',book:'osh',trigger:'Full Turn',adr:true,desc:'Your true powers only get revealed when you transform. You have two forms — one completely human, the other with incredible powers. While in human form you cannot access your Superpower or the Feats connected to it. When you transform, you regain access to all Superpowers and Feats on your Hero Sheet, and you may also move one Attribute Point of your choice (for example, from Focus to Brawn). Transformation requires a Full Turn. Quick Shift [Quick Action]: spend 1 Adrenaline to transform as a Quick Action and recover all Grit.'},
  {name:'Unlimited Funds',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',desc:'You’re not just rich, you are filthy rich. At character creation, you can spend 10$ on gear instead of 4, and then start the game with 5$. Once per Session, you can leverage your vast assets to gain access to exclusive services — a private jet, tickets to the most exclusive gala of the year, reserving a whole hotel, buying a restaurant to skip the line.',creationEffects:{cashOverride:5}},
  {name:'Unstoppable Force',book:'osh',trigger:'Quick Action',adr:true,desc:'You can use the incredible strength of your muscles or a manifestation of your powers to strike the enemy where it truly hurts. When you run or throw something at great speed, nothing can stop you. Devastating Attack [Quick Action]: spend 1 Adrenaline to gain +1 to your next Action Roll during combat. If you hit the Enemy, they lose 1 extra Grit. This special action can also be activated in combination with other special actions, like Smash! or Explosive Force.'},
  {name:'Wall-Climber',book:'osh',trigger:'Passive',desc:'You move like a spider, walking on walls and ceilings. You can climb and hang on any horizontal or vertical surface, and gain a Free Re-roll to all rolls made to climb.'}
];
const SUPERPOWERS_OSH=[
  {id:'hyper_armor',name:'Hyper-technological Armor',book:'osh',roleIds:['armored'],
   desc:'A suit of hyper-technological armor. Donning it requires a Full Turn. While worn, your Brawn is always 3 and you ignore all Hurt penalties. The armor grants Flight and lets you breathe underwater and in outer space. Outfitted with the Energy Beam super-weapon (Energy Weapon, Maximum Power) built into the hands or chest plate. You may spend Cash to bolt on additional weapons (submachine guns, swords, missile launchers, etc.). Free Re-roll to shoot the Energy Beam and any ranged weapon added to the armor. Recall [Quick Action]: in the open or near your suit, spend 1 Adrenaline to make it fly onto your body.'},
  {id:'natural_predator',name:'Natural Predator',book:'osh',roleIds:['beast'],
   desc:'You are a wild creature and share some features of an animal’s appearance or behavior. Free Re-roll to all Awareness rolls and to rolls made to follow tracks. Gain the Claws super-weapon (Melee Weapon, Sharp, attack with +1), extracted or retracted at will. Choose one Feat to gain: Acrobat, Wall-Climber, or Bulletproof.'},
  {id:'elemental_control',name:'Elemental Control',book:'osh',roleIds:['elemental'],
   desc:'Master one element (chosen below). So long as you are not Powerless, you are immune to damage from your element. Small or simple uses (lighting a candle, shaping an ice flower) need no roll; complex actions roll at the Director’s difficulty. Especially grand uses (raising an ice wall, summoning a tropical storm) may require spending Adrenaline at the Director’s call. Gain the Elemental Ray super-weapon (Energy Weapon). Elemental Form [Quick Action]: spend 1 Adrenaline to wreathe yourself in your element. Until end of combat or Scene, you fly as if you had the Flight Feat and gain a Free Re-roll using both your element and your Elemental Ray.',
   variants:[
     {id:'water',name:'Water',desc:'Pushes things, puts out fires, breaks barriers.'},
     {id:'electricity',name:'Electricity',desc:'Destroys obstacles, overloads technological devices.'},
     {id:'fire',name:'Fire',desc:'Burns wood and fabric, scares people, keeps enemies away.'},
     {id:'ice',name:'Ice',desc:'Freezes targets, makes surfaces slippery, creates barriers.'},
     {id:'storm',name:'Storm',desc:'Controls the weather and generates lightning.'},
     {id:'earth',name:'Earth',desc:'Builds platforms and barriers.'},
     {id:'wind',name:'Wind',desc:'Pushes objects and people away, blows out flames.'}
   ]},
  {id:'enhanced_body',name:'Enhanced Body',book:'osh',roleIds:['champion'],
   desc:'You are in more than perfect physical shape. Free Re-roll to all Brawn rolls; automatically gain the Trained Fighter Feat. I Can Do This All Day: once per Scene, when you lose more than 3 Grit at once, you gain 1 Adrenaline. You don’t need to spend Adrenaline to use this special action.'},
  {id:'force_control',name:'Force Control',book:'osh',roleIds:['force_master'],
   desc:'Telekinetically perceive and control your chosen force (below). Complex or tiring uses roll Focus+Cool with a Free Re-roll. Simple uses (moving a fork, opening a window) need no roll. Moving heavy or anchored objects may require spending Adrenaline at the Director’s call.',
   variants:[
     {id:'cosmic',name:'Cosmic Force',desc:'An invisible energy surrounding everything. Create flying platforms strong enough to hold a person, telekinetically move small items, or open distant doors. Additionally, raise small shields as a Quick Action — they grant protection like Partial Cover.'},
     {id:'electromagnetic',name:'Electromagnetic Force',desc:'Telekinetically control all ferromagnetic metals, like iron and steel.'}
   ]},
  {id:'incredible_strength',name:'Incredible Strength',book:'osh',roleIds:['tank'],
   desc:'Tall as two people, just as wide, muscle on stone-thick skin. +1 to all Force and Endure rolls; ignore all penalties and Conditions imposing -1 to Brawn rolls (unless Powerless). Always Help when rolling to crash, lift, throw, or break things; always Hindrance to go unnoticed or squeeze into narrow spaces. If your Superpower is always-on, gain the Monster Feat; if it is a reversible transformation, gain the Transformation Feat instead. Smash!: destroy an object or ride, or gain +2 to a Brawn roll.'},
  {id:'kinetic_energy',name:'Kinetic Energy',book:'osh',roleIds:['blaster'],
   desc:'Focus kinetic energy through a part of your body and release it as a devastating beam. Gain the Kinetic Ray super-weapon (Energy Weapon, Maximum Power, Impact); +1 and a Free Re-roll to shoot it. Explosive Force: +1 to rolls to attack with your Kinetic Ray, and your Kinetic Ray temporarily gains the Explosive Feat.'},
  {id:'mind_powers',name:'Mind Powers',book:'osh',roleIds:['psychic'],
   desc:'Telepathy in any language, telekinesis, and mental illusions. Complex uses roll Focus+Endure with a Free Re-roll. Read someone’s thoughts or locate a known person via Focus+Detect. Small uses (lifting a book, finding your flatmate at home) need no roll. Moving heavy objects or forcing an opponent to cooperate may require spending Adrenaline at the Director’s call. Whisper [Quick Action]: spend 1 Adrenaline to persuade a non-hostile individual, or to confuse an Enemy and grant +1 to an ally during combat.'},
  {id:'shapeshift',name:'Shapeshift',book:'osh',roleIds:['shapeshifter'],
   desc:'Choose one shapeshifter type (below). Regardless of type, you also gain Quick-Change. Quick-Change [Quick Action]: transform without spending a Full Turn.',
   variants:[
     {id:'humanoid',name:'Humanoid Shapeshifter',desc:'Turn into any humanoid, changing your appearance and voice completely. Base Skills unaltered; the new form can be a Help or Hindrance contextually. Transformation normally requires a Full Turn.'},
     {id:'animal',name:'Animal Shapeshifter',desc:'Turn into any animal. Base Skills unaltered; the form can be a Help or Hindrance contextually. Transformation normally requires a Full Turn.'},
     {id:'elastic',name:'Elastic Shapeshifter',desc:'Stretch and shrink like rubber. Help to all rolls to squeeze into narrow spaces, to catch or trap others, or to dodge bullets. You also take one additional Quick Action every Turn. Spend a Full Turn to inflate or stretch your body and significantly increase your size.'}
   ]},
  {id:'super_speed',name:'Super-Speed',book:'osh',roleIds:['speedster'],
   desc:'Free Re-roll to run, and +2 to all rolls made to chase, run away, or catch something before others do. You also take one additional Quick Action every Turn. Be Right Back [Full Turn]: spend the Turn to reach a spot you can run to, retrieve or drop something, and come back. You don’t need to spend Adrenaline to use this special action. In a Flash! [Quick Action]: once per Turn, if you are free from obstacles and able to move, spend 1 Adrenaline to take one of the following — run to any known place to take or leave an object or person; abandon combat and exit Enemy range; change clothes or don your super-suit; auto-succeed a Reaction Roll without rolling; or take a second Action Roll at -1 without any Free Re-roll.'},
  {id:'teleportation',name:'Teleportation',book:'osh',roleIds:['teleporter'],
   desc:'Teleport at will to any place you can see. Out of danger, focus for a Full Turn to teleport to any place on the planet you are familiar with or have visited before. Especially distant teleports may require spending Adrenaline at the Director’s call. Free Re-roll to all Reaction Rolls in combat, so long as you are not taken by surprise. Round Trip [Quick Action]: spend 1 Adrenaline to teleport to a place you know and can see, grab something, and come back right away. Group Teleport: spend 1 Adrenaline to teleport yourself and 1 other person.'},
  {id:'arcane_powers',name:'Arcane Powers',book:'osh',roleIds:['sorcerer'],
   desc:'You start the game with 2 Adrenaline instead of 1; at 0 Adrenaline you feel out of energy and cannot use your arcane powers. Summon small everyday objects (a pan, a rose, a fountain pen), conjure illusions, and telekinetically move unanchored objects as if with two invisible flying hands. Complex or tiring uses roll Smooth+Leadership with a Free Re-roll. Simple uses (summoning clothing, stirring a pot) need no roll. Especially complex or dangerous spells may require spending Adrenaline at the Director’s call. Choose one super-weapon: Magical Weapon (Melee Weapon, Perfect) or Arcane Missile (Energy Weapon), made of pure light, summoned or dismissed at will. Astral Projection [Full Turn]: spend 1 Adrenaline to create a projection of your body made of light — it can float, turn invisible, pass through solid surfaces, see, hear, and speak, but cannot interact with physical objects. Your physical body must remain still; the projection dissolves on lost focus, when you are struck, or when you are wounded.'},
  {id:'dark_presence',name:'Dark Presence',book:'osh',roleIds:['shadow'],
   desc:'A shadow in the alleys of your city — quiet as a cat, just as elusive. Free Re-roll to all Crime rolls, and +1 to all rolls made to ambush people or strike unaware Enemies. Vanish [Quick Action]: spend 1 Adrenaline to hide, get away from a thorny situation, break free from a grapple, or reach Partial or Total Cover. On the same Turn, you may spend an additional 1 Adrenaline to reappear in a nearby position you can see.'},
  {id:'battleborn',name:'Battleborn',book:'osh',roleIds:['weaponmaster'],
   desc:'Choose one weapon type: bows, guns, or melee weapons (below). Free Re-roll to use, repair, evaluate, or handle your chosen type of weapon. Plus the additional benefit listed under your chosen type.',
   variants:[
     {id:'guns',name:'Guns',desc:'You gain 2 Guns and 6 Mags for free. Once per Turn, reload a gun without using an action. When you shoot with two guns at the same time, you gain +1.'},
     {id:'bows',name:'Bows',desc:'You gain one Bow and 24 arrows for free. +1 to all rolls to shoot arrows. If you spend a Turn taking aim, gain an additional +1 to your next roll to shoot arrows.'},
     {id:'melee',name:'Melee Weapons',desc:'Choose one Melee Weapon (staff, katana, knives, etc.) and gain one weapon or a pair of weapons of your chosen type for free — they have the Perfect Feat. +1 to fight with your chosen weapon. When wielding a pair of melee weapons of the same type, gain +1 to dodge projectiles.'}
   ]},
  {id:'invincible',name:'Invincible',book:'osh',roleIds:['marvel'],
   autoFeats:['Flight','Energy Manipulation','Bulletproof','Only Weakness'],
   desc:'Marvel only — a practically perfect being. Free Re-roll to all Brawn rolls. Automatically gain the Flight, Energy Manipulation, Bulletproof, and Only Weakness Feats. At creation, gain 6 extra free Skill Points to assign freely (in addition to the 2 all Heroes get, for a total of 8).'},
  {id:'one_of_a_kind',name:'One of a Kind',book:'osh',roleIds:['prodigy'],
   desc:'Prodigy only — no other Hero is like you. Choose 1 Superpower and 1 Feat (or 2 Feats) from anything available. You may NOT choose Invincible unless it is absolutely crucial to the story and all other Players agree. At creation, gain 2 extra free Skill Points to assign freely (in addition to the 2 all Heroes get, for a total of 4).'},
  {id:'specialty',name:'Specialty',book:'osh',roleIds:['maverick'],
   desc:'You have no flashy powers, but a specialty makes you essential to the team. Choose one extra Feat of any kind from the Feat list — that is your Superpower. You begin the game with 2 Spotlights instead of 1. Underdog: repeat one roll of any kind; for this roll, you ignore all penalties imposed by Conditions other than Powerless.'}
];
